    <node id="Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)">
      <data key="d0">Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A method that empowers large language models to access external and private corpus, enabling factually consistent responses in specific domains.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6aab8177dccf033fdee79260a9b335ec</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/noderag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Graph-based RAG">
      <data key="d0">Graph-based RAG</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific approach within RAG that organizes textual information into an indexing graph to capture inherent dependencies and structured relationships, contrasting with flat-structured RAG methods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Flow-based pruning">
      <data key="d0">Flow-based pruning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An algorithm designed in PathRAG with distance awareness to identify and extract key relational paths between retrieved nodes, aiming to reduce redundant information and provide low time complexity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Path-based prompting">
      <data key="d0">Path-based prompting</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A strategy used in PathRAG where retrieved key relational paths are converted into textual form and sequentially concatenated into the prompt for LLMs, ordered by reliability scores to guide more logical and coherent responses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LightRAG">
      <data key="d0">LightRAG</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A RAG system known for its simple and fast approach, particularly its high-level key search methodology, which Zep's community search approach parallels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NaiveRAG">
      <data key="d0">NaiveRAG</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A baseline RAG method that divides documents into text chunks and retrieves based on vector similarity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6aab8177dccf033fdee79260a9b335ec</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/noderag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Text-based RAG">
      <data key="d0">Text-based RAG</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) approaches where external databases primarily store data in textual form, often organizing text segments in a flat structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sparse vector retrieval">
      <data key="d0">Sparse vector retrieval</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A retrieval mechanism in text-based RAG that typically identifies the most representative words in each text segment by word frequency and retrieves relevant text for a specific query based on keyword matching.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Dense vector retrieval">
      <data key="d0">Dense vector retrieval</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A retrieval mechanism in text-based RAG that addresses issues like lexical mismatches by encoding both query terms and text into vector embeddings, then retrieving relevant content based on their semantic similarity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Knowledge Graphs (KGs)">
      <data key="d0">Knowledge Graphs (KGs)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Data structures used to represent knowledge as a network of interconnected entities and their relationships. They are employed in Zep to enhance RAG architectures for LLM-agent memory.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KG-RAG">
      <data key="d0">KG-RAG</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A GraphRAG model tailored for the biomedical domain, leveraging specialized datasets and designed to link symptoms, diseases, and treatments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-73e6d6a5ae112be760116934a9ae4418</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/graphrag survey paper 2.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community detection algorithms">
      <data key="d0">Community detection algorithms</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Algorithms applied on graphs to identify groups of nodes that are more densely connected to each other than to the rest of the graph, used by GraphRAG to summarize information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ego-network information">
      <data key="d0">Ego-network information</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Refers to the immediate neighbors and connections of a specific node in a graph, used by LightRAG as retrieval results to simplify the retrieval process and handle global-level tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MiniRAG">
      <data key="d0">MiniRAG</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A concurrent work that leverages path information to assist retrieval, focusing on questions answerable by specific node information and exploring paths between query-related and answer-related nodes like KG reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Indexing graph">
      <data key="d0">Indexing graph</data>
      <data key="d1">data_structure</data>
      <data key="d2">A structured representation of a text database in graph-based RAG, where nodes represent distinct entities and edges represent relationships between entity pairs, serving as the knowledge source.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Resource allocation strategy">
      <data key="d0">Resource allocation strategy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A conceptual framework from which PathRAG's flow-based pruning algorithm was inspired, used to extract key paths by propagating resources through the graph.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Lost in the middle&quot; issue">
      <data key="d0">"Lost in the middle" issue</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A known phenomenon where Large Language Models tend to underperform when crucial information is placed in the middle of a long context, influencing PathRAG's prompt ordering strategy to place most critical information at the ends.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Comprehensiveness">
      <data key="d0">Comprehensiveness</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An evaluation criterion used in LLM-based multi-dimensional comparison, assessing how much detail an answer provides to cover all aspects of a question.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b56db976c18e50fdd3c10cb91d5939f</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/graphrag in unified framework.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720550</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Diversity">
      <data key="d0">Diversity</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An evaluation criterion used in LLM-based multi-dimensional comparison, assessing how varied and rich an answer is in providing different perspectives and insights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b56db976c18e50fdd3c10cb91d5939f</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/graphrag in unified framework.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720550</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Logicality">
      <data key="d0">Logicality</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An evaluation dimension used to assess how logically an LLM's answer responds to all parts of a question.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevance">
      <data key="d0">Relevance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An evaluation dimension used to assess how relevant an LLM's answer is to the question, staying focused and addressing the intended topic or issue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Coherence">
      <data key="d0">Coherence</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An evaluation dimension used to assess how well an LLM's answer maintains internal logical connections between its parts, ensuring a smooth and consistent structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="History dataset">
      <data key="d0">History dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">A dataset from the UltraDomain benchmark focusing on the field of history, covering various periods, events, and figures throughout time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biology dataset">
      <data key="d0">Biology dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">A dataset from the UltraDomain benchmark focusing on the field of biology, covering a wide range of topics such as plants, animals, and insects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b25520a9bfa83b9cad32ccb8f89d5538</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/pathrag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720133</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NodeRAG">
      <data key="d0">NodeRAG</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">The proposed graph-centric framework that introduces heterogeneous graph structures for seamless and holistic integration of graph-based methodologies into the RAG workflow.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6aab8177dccf033fdee79260a9b335ec</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/noderag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tianyang Xu">
      <data key="d0">Tianyang Xu</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An author of the paper, affiliated with Columbia University.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6aab8177dccf033fdee79260a9b335ec</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/noderag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Haojie Zheng">
      <data key="d0">Haojie Zheng</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An author of the paper, affiliated with the University of Pennsylvania.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6aab8177dccf033fdee79260a9b335ec</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/noderag.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chengze Li">
