    </node>
    <node id="Daniel Chalef">
      <data key="d0">Daniel Chalef</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An author of the paper, affiliated with Zep AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Zep AI">
      <data key="d0">Zep AI</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The organization that developed the Zep memory layer service and employs the authors of the paper.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MemGPT">
      <data key="d0">MemGPT</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A state-of-the-art memory system for Large Language Models (LLMs), serving as a primary baseline for comparison with Zep in memory retrieval benchmarks. It was introduced by Charles Packer et al.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deep Memory Retrieval (DMR) benchmark">
      <data key="d0">Deep Memory Retrieval (DMR) benchmark</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">A benchmark for evaluating LLM memory systems, established by the MemGPT team. It comprises 500 multi-session conversations from the Multi-Session Chat dataset.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LongMemEval benchmark">
      <data key="d0">LongMemEval benchmark</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">A comprehensive and challenging benchmark for evaluating chat assistants on long-term interactive memory. It features longer conversations and diverse question types reflective of real-world enterprise use cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transformer-based models">
      <data key="d0">Transformer-based models</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of neural network architecture that forms the foundation of many modern Large Language Models (LLMs), known for processing sequential data and capturing long-range dependencies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Information Retrieval (IR)">
      <data key="d0">Information Retrieval (IR)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Techniques developed over decades, leveraged by Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to provide domain knowledge to Large Language Models (LLMs).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Episode Subgraph">
      <data key="d0">Episode Subgraph</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">One of three hierarchical tiers in Zep's knowledge graph, serving as a non-lossy data store for raw input data (messages, text, JSON) from which semantic entities and relations are extracted. It mirrors psychological models of human episodic memory.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Semantic Entity Subgraph">
      <data key="d0">Semantic Entity Subgraph</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">One of three hierarchical tiers in Zep's knowledge graph, built upon the episode subgraph. It contains entity nodes and edges representing relationships between entities extracted and resolved from episodes, mirroring human semantic memory.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Subgraph">
      <data key="d0">Community Subgraph</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The highest level of Zep's knowledge graph, representing clusters of strongly connected entities. Community nodes contain high-level summarizations, offering a comprehensive view of the semantic entity subgraph's structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bi-temporal model">
      <data key="d0">Bi-temporal model</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An approach implemented in Zep for managing dynamic temporal information by tracking two distinct timelines: one for the chronological ordering of events (T) and another for the transactional order of data ingestion (T').</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Entity extraction">
      <data key="d0">Entity extraction</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The initial phase of episode processing in Zep, where named entities are identified from current and previous message content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reflection technique">
      <data key="d0">Reflection technique</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A technique employed in Zep's entity extraction process, inspired by Reflexion, to minimize hallucinations and enhance extraction coverage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Entity resolution">
      <data key="d0">Entity resolution</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A process in Zep that identifies and resolves duplicate entities extracted from conversations by comparing new entities with existing graph entities using embeddings and full-text search.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cypher queries">
      <data key="d0">Cypher queries</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A declarative graph query language used in Zep to incorporate extracted data into the knowledge graph, chosen to ensure consistent schema formats and reduce potential hallucinations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fact extraction">
      <data key="d0">Fact extraction</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The process of identifying and extracting factual statements and their key predicates between different entities from the episode context in Zep's knowledge graph construction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Edge invalidation">
      <data key="d0">Edge invalidation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A key feature of Graphiti where existing edges in the knowledge graph are marked as invalid when new, contradictory temporal information is introduced, ensuring the graph reflects current states while maintaining historical records.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community detection">
      <data key="d0">Community detection</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A process that constructs the community subgraph in Zep by clustering strongly connected entities, building upon techniques described in GraphRAG.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Label propagation algorithm">
      <data key="d0">Label propagation algorithm</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An algorithm used by Zep for community detection, chosen for its straightforward dynamic extension that helps maintain accurate community representations as new data enters the graph.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)">
      <data key="d0">Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A reranking approach supported by Zep's memory retrieval system to increase precision by combining ranked lists from different search methods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Maximal Marginal Relevance (MMR)">
      <data key="d0">Maximal Marginal Relevance (MMR)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A reranking approach supported by Zep's memory retrieval system, used to increase precision by optimizing for relevance while minimizing redundancy in search results.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Graph-based episode-mentions reranker">
      <data key="d0">Graph-based episode-mentions reranker</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A reranker implemented by Zep that prioritizes search results based on the frequency of entity or fact mentions within a conversation, making frequently referenced information more readily accessible.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Node distance reranker">
      <data key="d0">Node distance reranker</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A reranker implemented by Zep that reorders results based on their graph distance from a designated centroid node, providing context localized to specific areas of the knowledge graph.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cross-encoders">
      <data key="d0">Cross-encoders</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of Large Language Model (LLM) used in Zep's sophisticated reranking capability that generates relevance scores by evaluating nodes and edges against queries using cross-attention, albeit with high computational cost.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cosine semantic similarity search">
      <data key="d0">Cosine semantic similarity search</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">One of the three search functions implemented by Zep, used to identify relevant documents by capturing semantic similarities between embeddings, often relying on Neo4j's Lucene implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Okapi BM25 full-text search">
      <data key="d0">Okapi BM25 full-text search</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">One of the three search functions implemented by Zep, used to identify relevant documents by measuring word similarities in full-text content, often relying on Neo4j's Lucene implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Breadth-first search (BFS)">
      <data key="d0">Breadth-first search (BFS)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">One of the three search functions implemented by Zep, used over knowledge graphs to enhance initial search results by identifying additional nodes and edges within n-hops, revealing contextual similarities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Apache Lucene">
      <data key="d0">Apache Lucene</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">An open-source search engine library whose implementation is utilized by Neo4j within Zep for features like cosine semantic similarity search and Okapi BM25 full-text search.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Session Chat dataset">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Session Chat dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">A dataset introduced in 'Beyond Goldfish Memory: Long-Term Open-Domain Conversation', a 500-conversation subset of which is used in the Deep Memory Retrieval (DMR) task.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BAAI">
      <data key="d0">BAAI</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Beijing Academy of Artificial Intelligence, the organization that developed the BGE-m3 models used by Zep for reranking and embedding tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BGE-m3 models">
      <data key="d0">BGE-m3 models</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">Specific models developed by BAAI used by Zep for both reranking and embedding tasks in its experimental implementation due to their multi-lingual, multi-functionality, and multi-granularity capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18">
      <data key="d0">gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific version of an OpenAI Large Language Model used by Zep for graph construction and for the chat agent generating responses in experiments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="gpt-4o-2024-11-20">
      <data key="d0">gpt-4o-2024-11-20</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific, more capable version of an OpenAI Large Language Model used by Zep for the chat agent generating responses in experiments, demonstrating improved performance with Zep.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09">
      <data key="d0">gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific version of an OpenAI Large Language Model used for conducting the Deep Memory Retrieval (DMR) evaluation to ensure direct comparability with MemGPT’s reported results.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AriGraph">
      <data key="d0">AriGraph</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A graph-based RAG system that uses distinct episodic and semantic subgraphs, an approach from which Zep's design draws inspiration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distill-SynthKG">
      <data key="d0">Distill-SynthKG</data>
      <data key="d1">technology</data>
      <data key="d2">A graph-based RAG system mentioned as a notable example of the limited application of breadth-first search in the RAG domain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FinanceBench">
      <data key="d0">FinanceBench</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">A benchmark for financial question answering, mentioned as an example of established RAG benchmarks against which Zep's traditional RAG capabilities could be evaluated in future work.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BEIR">
      <data key="d0">BEIR</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">A heterogeneous benchmark for zero-shot evaluation of information retrieval models, mentioned as an example of established RAG benchmarks against which Zep's traditional RAG capabilities could be evaluated in future work.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Charles Packer">
      <data key="d0">Charles Packer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lead author of the paper introducing MemGPT and the Deep Memory Retrieval (DMR) task.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Di Wu">
      <data key="d0">Di Wu</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Lead author of the paper introducing the LongMemEval benchmark and dataset.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Episodic memory">
      <data key="d0">Episodic memory</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A psychological model of human memory that represents distinct events, mirrored by Zep's Episode Subgraph.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Semantic memory">
      <data key="d0">Semantic memory</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A psychological model of human memory that captures associations between concepts and their meanings, mirrored by Zep's Semantic Entity Subgraph.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Formal ontologies">
      <data key="d0">Formal ontologies</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Structured representations of knowledge domains, foundational in pre-LLM knowledge graph work, suggested as a promising area for further exploration within the Graphiti framework for LLM-generated KGs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abd9a1af6fbc0228958274294f75bef7</data>
      <data key="d4">pdfs/graphrag/zep graphiti.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1753720603</data>
    </node>
